# Discover a source's schema

Reads the tables and columns of a live RDBMS source connection, so a data flow's schema mapping
comes from the real source instead of being hand-written and left to drift.

## How it works

`{{.Name}}` drives the same discovery the console's mapping tab uses: the platform opens a connection
to the source, introspects the requested schema (and, if you name them, specific tables), and returns
the columns.

- `schemas_json` — a ready-to-use `properties.schemas[]` block. Decode it with `jsondecode()` straight
  into a data flow's `properties_json` — see the example below.
- `schemas` — the same discovery exposed as typed nested objects, for inspecting the result instead of
  decoding raw JSON.

RDBMS sources only today (MySQL, PostgreSQL, SQL Server, Oracle, …) — there is no equivalent
discovery path yet for SaaS/API connectors.

